  "geometryBasis": "The named Anping Tree House precinct, separate Tait merchant house and both mapped wooden paths define site identity and surroundings. The estimated outline places the five warehouse sections immediately north of the merchant house with the published total warehouse area of roughly 1,322 m².",
  "sectionBasis": "The city operator describes banyans growing through the former warehouse walls and roof and the elevated wooden walkways. The restoration architect’s interview records five warehouse sections, three banyan groups, three square black mesh lookout platforms, and remnants of red brick and granite openings.",
  "limitations": [
    "The garden boundary and outside paths come from the native map. Individual warehouse outlines, internal layout, wall heights, and the placement and profiles of roots and canopies are estimates using the published aggregate area and descriptions.",
    "The modern wooden visitor walk, stairs and three black steel platforms are reconstructed at representative positions inside the surviving warehouse sector. The mapped continuation to the north gives the exit bearing. Fine roof remnants, mortar color and rail details are approximate.",
    "The separately named merchant house, former residence, cafe, garden attractions and landscape beyond the old warehouse are outside scope."
